The exploits produced with an LLM during the disclosure window worked only against non-PIE builds, first without and then with ASLR; the exploit against the default PIE build was the human researcher's. The Exim maintainers know no mitigation other than upgrading to 4.99.3, so disabling CHUNKING advertisement is not a vendor workaround, and the advisory sets the CVSS 9.8 and the affected range of 4.97 to 4.99.2 on builds with GnuTLS.
